{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"8b91ac87"},"source":["# 3 — El bloque Transformer completo\n","\n","Último notebook. Sobre el **Notebook 2** (multi-head attention) agregamos las tres piezas que faltan para tener un Transformer de verdad:\n","\n","1. **Feed-forward** — el cómputo por token (lo que la atención no hace).\n","2. **El bloque** — atención + feed-forward, con **residuales** y **LayerNorm**, que hacen entrenable la profundidad.\n","3. **Apilar** `N` bloques → el modelo completo.\n","\n","Autocontenido: la Sección 0 repite el setup. `Head` y `MultiHeadAttention` son las del Notebook 2 — acá sólo les sumamos *dropout*."],"id":"8b91ac87"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1480bb13"},"source":["## Sección 0 — Setup\n","\n","Mismo setup de siempre, con dos cambios: **hiperparámetros más grandes** (el modelo ahora es profundo) y **dropout** — una regularización que apaga al azar una fracción de las activaciones durante el entrenamiento, para que el modelo no memorice."],"id":"1480bb13"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"9d99584a","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454439853,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":325,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"97abeaf1-b63a-4c6d-9466-2d737c640a7e"},"source":["!wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt"],"id":"9d99584a","execution_count":1,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["--2026-08-11 13:20:39--  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt\n","Resolving raw.githubusercontent.com (raw.githubusercontent.com)... 185.199.108.133, 185.199.109.133, 185.199.110.133, ...\n","Connecting to raw.githubusercontent.com (raw.githubusercontent.com)|185.199.108.133|:443... connected.\n","HTTP request sent, awaiting response... 200 OK\n","Length: 1115394 (1.1M) [text/plain]\n","Saving to: ‘input.txt’\n","\n","\rinput.txt             0%[                    ]       0  --.-KB/s               \rinput.txt           100%[===================>]   1.06M  --.-KB/s    in 0.03s   \n","\n","2026-08-11 13:20:39 (34.0 MB/s) - ‘input.txt’ saved [1115394/1115394]\n","\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"ff22f518","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447337,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":7459,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"810e5228-510a-44cf-c4bb-20eb0ddf79b2"},"source":["import torch\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","from torch.nn import functional as F\n","\n","torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","device = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\n","print('device:', device)"],"id":"ff22f518","execution_count":2,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["device: cuda\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"8039a24d","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447511,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":163,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["with open('input.txt', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n","    text = f.read()\n","\n","chars = sorted(list(set(text)))\n","vocab_size = len(chars)\n","\n","stoi = { ch:i for i,ch in enumerate(chars) }\n","itos = { i:ch for i,ch in enumerate(chars) }\n","encode = lambda s: [stoi[c] for c in s]\n","decode = lambda l: ''.join([itos[i] for i in l])\n","\n","data = torch.tensor(encode(text), dtype=torch.long)\n","n = int(0.9*len(data))\n","train_data, val_data = data[:n], data[n:]"],"id":"8039a24d","execution_count":3,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"6ca8ad7e","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447609,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":96,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["# hiperparámetros (más grandes: el modelo ahora es profundo)\n","batch_size    = 16\n","block_size    = 32\n","n_embd        = 64\n","n_head        = 4\n","n_layer       = 4      # cuántos bloques Transformer apilamos\n","dropout       = 0.1\n","learning_rate = 1e-3\n","max_iters     = 10000\n","eval_interval = 500\n","eval_iters    = 200\n","\n","def get_batch(split):\n","    d = train_data if split == 'train' else val_data\n","    ix = torch.randint(len(d) - block_size, (batch_size,))\n","    x = torch.stack([d[i:i+block_size]     for i in ix])\n","    y = torch.stack([d[i+1:i+block_size+1] for i in ix])\n","    return x.to(device), y.to(device)\n","\n","@torch.no_grad()\n","def estimate_loss(model):\n","    out = {}\n","    model.eval()\n","    for split in ['train', 'val']:\n","        losses = torch.zeros(eval_iters)\n","        for k in range(eval_iters):\n","            X, Y = get_batch(split)\n","            _, loss = model(X, Y)\n","            losses[k] = loss.item()\n","        out[split] = losses.mean().item()\n","    model.train()\n","    return out\n","\n","def train(model, max_iters=max_iters):\n","    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=learning_rate)\n","    for it in range(max_iters):\n","        if it % eval_interval == 0 or it == max_iters - 1:\n","            l = estimate_loss(model)\n","            print(f\"step {it:4d}: train loss {l['train']:.4f}, val loss {l['val']:.4f}\")\n","        xb, yb = get_batch('train')\n","        _, loss = model(xb, yb)\n","        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n","        loss.backward()\n","        optimizer.step()\n","    return model"],"id":"6ca8ad7e","execution_count":4,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"362e2e5d"},"source":["## Sección 1 — Las piezas del Notebook 2 (+ dropout)\n","\n","`Head` y `MultiHeadAttention` ya las construimos. Las repetimos para que el notebook corra solo, con un único agregado: una capa de **dropout**. `MultiHeadAttention` sigue siendo *concat + proyección `W_O`*."],"id":"362e2e5d"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"d3782aa2","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447616,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":4,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["class Head(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\" una cabeza de self-attention \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, head_size):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.key   = nn.Linear(n_embd, head_size, bias=False)\n","        self.query = nn.Linear(n_embd, head_size, bias=False)\n","        self.value = nn.Linear(n_embd, head_size, bias=False)\n","        self.register_buffer('tril', torch.tril(torch.ones(block_size, block_size)))\n","        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\n","\n","    def forward(self, x):\n","        B, T, C = x.shape\n","        k = self.key(x)     # (B,T,head_size)\n","        q = self.query(x)   # (B,T,head_size)\n","        wei = q @ k.transpose(-2, -1) * k.shape[-1]**-0.5              # (B,T,T)  afinidades / √(head_size)\n","        wei = wei.masked_fill(self.tril[:T, :T] == 0, float('-inf'))  # máscara causal\n","        wei = F.softmax(wei, dim=-1)\n","        wei = self.dropout(wei)\n","        v = self.value(x)   # (B,T,head_size)\n","        return wei @ v      # (B,T,head_size)"],"id":"d3782aa2","execution_count":5,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"7f91b6b9","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447618,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":1,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["class MultiHeadAttention(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\" varias cabezas en paralelo: concat + proyección W_O \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, num_heads, head_size):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.heads = nn.ModuleList([Head(head_size) for _ in range(num_heads)])\n","        self.proj  = nn.Linear(n_embd, n_embd)   # W_O: mezcla las cabezas\n","        self.dropout = nn.Dropout(dropout)\n","\n","    def forward(self, x):\n","        out = torch.cat([h(x) for h in self.heads], dim=-1)   # (B,T,n_embd)\n","        return self.dropout(self.proj(out))                    # (B,T,n_embd)"],"id":"7f91b6b9","execution_count":6,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1f63478a"},"source":["## Sección 2 — Feed-forward: cómputo por token\n","\n","La atención **comunica** los tokens (los mezcla), pero no los **procesa**: después de mezclar, falta una etapa que tome cada token por separado y lo transforme. Es un MLP pequeño con una no-linealidad —`Linear → ReLU → Linear`— con una capa oculta ancha (`4 × n_embd`), aplicado a cada posición de forma independiente."],"id":"1f63478a"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"165bc856","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447668,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":49,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["class FeedForward(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\" Linear -> ReLU -> Linear, aplicado a cada token por separado \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, n_embd):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Linear(n_embd, 4 * n_embd),   # expande\n","            nn.ReLU(),                       # no-linealidad\n","            nn.Linear(4 * n_embd, n_embd),   # vuelve a n_embd\n","            nn.Dropout(dropout),\n","        )\n","\n","    def forward(self, x):\n","        return self.net(x)   # (B,T,n_embd)"],"id":"165bc856","execution_count":7,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"7e3abe0c"},"source":["## Sección 3 — El bloque: comunicación + cómputo\n","\n","Queremos apilar muchas capas de (atención + feed-forward), pero apilar en profundidad, por sí solo, hace que el gradiente se desvanezca y el modelo no entrene. Dos mecanismos lo arreglan:\n","\n","- **Residual** — `x = x + sublayer(x)`: suma la entrada a la salida, dándole al gradiente un camino directo hacia atrás.\n","- **LayerNorm** — normaliza cada vector (media 0, varianza 1) para mantener las activaciones en escala estable.\n","\n","Un **bloque** es entonces: **comunicación** (multi-head) y después **cómputo** (feed-forward), cada uno envuelto en su LayerNorm y su residual. Usamos *pre-norm*: la norma va **antes** de cada sub-bloque."],"id":"7e3abe0c"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"9927efd8","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447670,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":3,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["class Block(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\" bloque Transformer: comunicación (atención) seguida de cómputo (FFN) \"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, n_embd, n_head):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        head_size = n_embd // n_head\n","        self.sa   = MultiHeadAttention(n_head, head_size)\n","        self.ffwd = FeedForward(n_embd)\n","        self.ln1  = nn.LayerNorm(n_embd)\n","        self.ln2  = nn.LayerNorm(n_embd)\n","\n","    def forward(self, x):\n","        x = x + self.sa(self.ln1(x))     # comunicación  (+ residual)\n","        x = x + self.ffwd(self.ln2(x))   # cómputo        (+ residual)\n","        return x"],"id":"9927efd8","execution_count":8,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2d32d0c8"},"source":["## Sección 4 — El modelo completo\n","\n","Apilamos `N = n_layer` bloques, una LayerNorm final y la `lm_head` que produce los logits. El flujo entero:\n","\n","`tokens → embedding + posición → (bloque) × N → LayerNorm → lm_head → logits`\n","\n","Ya no es un bigrama: es un **GPT** (un Transformer decoder-only). La generación es autoregresiva, recortando el contexto a `block_size`."],"id":"2d32d0c8"},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"a06a11cb","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454447681,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":10,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}}},"source":["class GPTLanguageModel(nn.Module):\n","\n","    def __init__(self):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.token_embedding_table    = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, n_embd)\n","        self.position_embedding_table = nn.Embedding(block_size, n_embd)\n","        self.blocks  = nn.Sequential(*[Block(n_embd, n_head=n_head) for _ in range(n_layer)])\n","        self.ln_f    = nn.LayerNorm(n_embd)          # LayerNorm final\n","        self.lm_head = nn.Linear(n_embd, vocab_size)\n","\n","    def forward(self, idx, targets=None):\n","        B, T = idx.shape\n","        tok_emb = self.token_embedding_table(idx)                                    # (B,T,n_embd)\n","        pos_emb = self.position_embedding_table(torch.arange(T, device=idx.device))  # (T,n_embd)\n","        x = tok_emb + pos_emb                                                        # (B,T,n_embd)\n","        x = self.blocks(x)                                                           # (B,T,n_embd)\n","        x = self.ln_f(x)                                                             # (B,T,n_embd)\n","        logits = self.lm_head(x)                                                     # (B,T,vocab_size)\n","\n","        loss = None\n","        if targets is not None:\n","            B, T, C = logits.shape\n","            logits  = logits.view(B*T, C)\n","            targets = targets.view(B*T)\n","            loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, targets)\n","        return logits, loss\n","\n","    def generate(self, idx, max_new_tokens):\n","        for _ in range(max_new_tokens):\n","            idx_cond = idx[:, -block_size:]          # recorte a block_size\n","            logits, _ = self(idx_cond)\n","            logits = logits[:, -1, :]                # último paso -> (B, vocab_size)\n","            probs = F.softmax(logits, dim=-1)\n","            idx_next = torch.multinomial(probs, num_samples=1)\n","            idx = torch.cat((idx, idx_next), dim=1)\n","        return idx"],"id":"a06a11cb","execution_count":9,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"2d4b4d42","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1786454762444,"user_tz":180,"elapsed":314762,"user":{"displayName":"Francisco Traversaro","userId":"11717466918051452843"}},"outputId":"21e57630-f5dc-45bb-bf07-eb6ee20a7a60"},"source":["torch.manual_seed(1337)\n","model = GPTLanguageModel().to(device)\n","print(sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())/1e3, 'K parámetros')\n","train(model)"],"id":"2d4b4d42","execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["0.209729 M parámetros\n","step    0: train loss 4.4109, val loss 4.4016\n","step  500: train loss 2.2986, val loss 2.2977\n","step 1000: train loss 2.1028, val loss 2.1251\n","step 1500: train loss 1.9875, val loss 2.0458\n","step 2000: train loss 1.9170, val loss 1.9895\n","step 2500: train loss 1.8623, val loss 1.9610\n","step 3000: train loss 1.8186, val loss 1.9325\n","step 3500: train loss 1.7986, val loss 1.9168\n","step 4000: train loss 1.7670, val loss 1.8887\n","step 4500: train loss 1.7475, val loss 1.8934\n","step 5000: train loss 1.7183, val loss 1.8702\n","step 5500: train loss 1.7023, val loss 1.8508\n","step 6000: train loss 1.6936, val loss 1.8530\n","step 6500: train loss 1.6805, val loss 1.8179\n","step 7000: train loss 1.6586, val loss 1.8249\n","step 7500: train loss 1.6564, val loss 1.8185\n","step 8000: train loss 1.6551, val loss 1.8364\n","step 8500: train loss 1.6292, val loss 1.7986\n","step 9000: train loss 1.6310, val loss 1.8026\n","step 9500: train loss 1.6277, val loss 1.8049\n","step 9999: train loss 1.6006, val loss 1.7896\n"]},{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["GPTLanguageModel(\n","  (token_embedding_table): Embedding(65, 64)\n","  (position_embedding_table): Embedding(32, 64)\n","  (blocks): Sequential(\n","    (0): Block(\n","      (sa): MultiHeadAttention(\n","        (heads): ModuleList(\n","          (0-3): 4 x Head(\n","            (key): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (query): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (value): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (dropout): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","          )\n","        )\n","        (proj): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=64, bias=True)\n","        (dropout): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","      )\n","      (ffwd): FeedForward(\n","        (net): Sequential(\n","          (0): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=256, bias=True)\n","          (1): ReLU()\n","          (2): Linear(in_features=256, out_features=64, bias=True)\n","          (3): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","        )\n","      )\n","      (ln1): LayerNorm((64,), eps=1e-05, elementwise_affine=True)\n","      (ln2): LayerNorm((64,), eps=1e-05, elementwise_affine=True)\n","    )\n","    (1): Block(\n","      (sa): MultiHeadAttention(\n","        (heads): ModuleList(\n","          (0-3): 4 x Head(\n","            (key): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (query): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (value): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (dropout): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","          )\n","        )\n","        (proj): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=64, bias=True)\n","        (dropout): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","      )\n","      (ffwd): FeedForward(\n","        (net): Sequential(\n","          (0): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=256, bias=True)\n","          (1): ReLU()\n","          (2): Linear(in_features=256, out_features=64, bias=True)\n","          (3): Dropout(p=0.1, inplace=False)\n","        )\n","      )\n","      (ln1): LayerNorm((64,), eps=1e-05, elementwise_affine=True)\n","      (ln2): LayerNorm((64,), eps=1e-05, elementwise_affine=True)\n","    )\n","    (2): Block(\n","      (sa): MultiHeadAttention(\n","        (heads): ModuleList(\n","          (0-3): 4 x Head(\n","            (key): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, bias=False)\n","            (query): Linear(in_features=64, out_features=16, b